<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>‚àí</mo><mo>‚à´</mo><mi>œÅ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>‚Å°</mo><mi>œÅ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>‚Äâ</mtext><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(x,t) = - \int \rho(x,t) \log \rho(x,t) \, dx</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.2222em; vertical-align: -0.8622em;"></span><span class="mord">‚àí</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op" style="margin-right: 0.44445em; position: relative; top: -0.0011em;">‚à´</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">œÅ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">œÅ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span></span></span></span></span>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Where:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
\item $D_\Phi$ = diffusion coefficient (spreads stress across neighbors)
\item $\alpha$ = damping of extreme spikes (taxation, anti-gambling)
\item $\beta$ = individual-level external pressures (housing, jobs)
\item $\mathcal{I}(x,t)$ = individual shocks
\item $\gamma$ = response of agency to stress gradient
\item $\eta$ = self-organization of vector flow
\item $\zeta \mathcal{F}_{\text{policy}}$ = external field intervention (e.g., geozotic families, community lotteries)
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Inspired by advanced field theories, these equations capture social dynamics analogous to physical systems \citep{ptvv2013shifted, bertacca2025entropic}.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\subsection{Scenario 1: Current Founder-Individual System}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\textbf{Parameters:}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
\item High $\beta$, low $\alpha$ $\rightarrow$ individual pressures dominate, little damping
\item $D_\Phi$ small $\rightarrow$ poor diffusion, stress localized
\item $\zeta = 0$ $\rightarrow$ no collective interventions
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\textbf{Behavior:}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
\item Scalar field $\Phi$ shows sharp, high-gradient spikes at individual nodes (households)
\item Vector field $\mathcal{V}$ is chaotic and fragmented; agents‚Äô effort vectors misaligned
\item Entropy $S$ is low locally but high globally, as stress concentrates unpredictably
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\textbf{Interpretation:}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
\item Each household acts as a singular high-energy attractor
\item Hyper-fragmentation of agency flows
\item System is brittle: small shocks can propagate disproportionately \citep{thompson1963making}
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\subsection{Scenario 2: Radical RSVP Interventions}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\textbf{Parameters:}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
\item Reduce $\beta$ (stress relief via housing/childcare support)
\item Increase $\alpha$ (progressive taxation, anti-gambling)
\item Increase $D_\Phi$ (community integration, geozotic households)
\item $\zeta \neq 0$ (futarchy-inspired policies, community lotteries)
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\textbf{Behavior:}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
\item Scalar field $\Phi$ smooths into distributed minima: stress spikes reduced
\item Vector field $\mathcal{V}$ aligns with field gradients, forming coherent flow manifolds
\item Entropy $S$ increases but is structured: distributed and usable for resilience
\end{itemize}</p>
