<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span>**2. Vector Field $\mathcal{V}(x,t)$**</span></p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Represents flow of influence, wealth, or social energy between nodes:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">‚àá</mi><mo>‚ãÖ</mo><mi mathvariant="script">V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>œÅ</mi><mtext>sources</mtext></msub><mo>‚àí</mo><msub><mi>œÅ</mi><mtext>sinks</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla \cdot \mathcal{V} = \rho_{\text{sources}} - \rho_{\text{sinks}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">‚àá</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">‚ãÖ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08222em;">V</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">œÅ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">sources</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">‚àí</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">œÅ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">sinks</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span>**RSVP Interpretation:**</span></p>
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words">Divergence ($\nabla \cdot \mathcal{V} &gt; 0$) ‚Üí outgoing influence from a node (e.g., wealth redistribution).</li>
<li class="break-words">Curl ($\nabla \times \mathcal{V} \neq 0$) ‚Üí cyclic social dynamics, e.g., cultural loops.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span>**Boundary Conditions:**</span></p>
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words">At singular attractors (celebrity nodes):
&nbsp;&nbsp;$\Phi \to \Phi_{\text{max}}, \quad \nabla \Phi \to 0$ outside distributed nodes.</li>
<li class="break-words">Geozotic families: distributed minima of $\Phi$ create coherent social wells.</li>
</ul>
