<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\frac{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\partial</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> S}{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\partial</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> t} + </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \cdot</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \mathbf{J}_S = </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\sigma</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">(x,t)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">equation</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">where </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathbf{J}_S</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> is entropy flux and </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\sigma</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">(x,t)</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> is local generation.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Boundary conditions at singular attractors (e.g., celebrity nodes): </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \to </span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">_{\text{max}}</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">, </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);"> \Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> \to </span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> outside distributed nodes. For geozotic families, distributed minima create coherent social wells.</span></span>
